From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:42:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Mythic: free_async_queue UAF fix + wineserver
 fd-ownership/kill tracing

server/async.c -- free_async_queue: unlink the queue entry AND list_init it.
The saga cost two runs: a bare list_remove crashed ml580 in req_cancel_async,
but REMOVING it was worse -- ml581 took the first c0000020 in 227 logs, because
surviving asyncs stayed linked into the dying struct fd's queue head, a sibling
unlink then clobbered the recycled fd's unix_fd, and the short PE-header pread
surfaced as "failed to load steamui.dll" (the mixed-arch fallback never fires
on c0000020). list_remove + list_init makes the node a singleton so a later
unlink only writes to itself. Disasm-verified in the shipped dylib.

server/thread.c, server/process.c -- ml586 [srv-kill]/[srv-own] tracing for the
0060-family kills, where one pseudo-process's teardown takes down another's
wineserver comm fds (services.exe loses its rpcrt4 listener -> SCM RPC dies ->
explorer wedges in OpenSCManagerW -> no Start menu; 8/8 run correlation).
Four previously SILENT paths now log: thread_poll_event's single-thread HUP
kill, kill_thread, kill_process (with its full thread list), and
process_poll_event; plus new_thread/init_thread ownership (which process a
thread files under, and the client-fd -> server-dup mapping).

Also carries the earlier #79 TCP-state and render-probe work.

(cherry picked from commit f2fa8d3b883bb59ae2bacc3d16cb6bf5d193d099)
